      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is the importance of particle size in physical zinc oxide sunscreens?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Particle size dictates both the aesthetic transparency and the optical protection profile. Standard pigment-grade zinc oxide has large particles (exceeding 200 nm) that scatter visible light, leaving a thick, opaque white cast on the skin. Micronized or nano-grade zinc oxide (particle size of 20 to 100 nm) reduces visible light scattering, making the formula transparent on skin, while maintaining a high band-gap absorption capacity for both UVA and UVB rays."
      }
    },
